---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="A little about Frank Trout and this blog."
	pubDate={new Date('June 06 2026')}
>
	<img class="avatar" src="/profile.jpg" alt="Frank Trout" width="120" height="120" />

	<p>
		Hi, I'm Frank Trout. After 25 years in IT, most of it in cybersecurity, I build AI tooling
		for a security team — triage helpers, evaluation harnesses, and the unglamorous plumbing
		underneath. It has to be right, because somebody puts their name on the output.
	</p>

	<p>
		This is where I write that up: agent loops and the failures that don't raise anything, tool
		use, evaluation, context, and what any of it actually costs to run. Every post with code in
		it ships with a single file you can run — one dependency, nothing to provision.
	</p>

	<p>
		These are notes on what I ran into, not claims about how it ought to be done. I've picked
		the wrong tool, kept the wrong abstraction too long, and shipped things I had to take
		apart again. Where that happened I'd rather say so than tidy it up afterwards.
	</p>

	<p>
		You can find my code on <a href="https://github.com/ftrout">GitHub</a> or
		<a href="/rss.xml">subscribe to the blog via RSS</a>. Thanks for reading.
	</p>

	<style>
		.avatar {
			width: 120px;
			height: 120px;
			border-radius: 50%;
			object-fit: cover;
			border: 1px solid rgb(var(--border));
			margin: 0 0 var(--space-m) 0;
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
